  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important first step is to establish a simple, fast-to-train baseline that anchors all future comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: it uses a standard linear encoder (PCA), a single profile, and no aggregation or fusion, making it quick to train and easy to interpret. It will give me a reference validation accuracy for the RNA modality under the most basic setting. This baseline is essential because every subsequent experiment—whether testing better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), adding image modality, or trying multiprofile aggregation—needs a clear reference point to measure improvement against. Starting with the simplest model also avoids confounding multiple design choices simultaneously, and with 9 experiments remaining, I can systematically build complexity from this anchor."
